-- DB update 2026_09_10_13 -> 2026_09_10_14
-- Arcane Mage rework (docs/arcane-mage-rework-design.md) - playtest bugfix pass, part 3
-- (2026-09-09, follow-up to rev_1788923279464564992.sql), see
-- .claude/skills/class-rework/SKILL.md.
--
-- 36032 ("Arcane Blast", the real stock stacking self-buff cast by spell_mage_arcane_blast's own
-- AfterCast hook): drops the ProcChance/ProcCharges/ProcTypeMask (100/1/65536) raw_overrides added
-- in Phase 3 Batch A. They were never needed - the buff's stacking is driven entirely by
-- CastSpell from Arcane Blast's own recast, not by any native proc - but they turned out to be
-- live: `spell_proc`'s own explicit row for 36032 has ProcFlags=0, which SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs()
-- treats as a sentinel meaning "fall back to spell_dbc's own ProcFlags/ProcChance/ProcCharges",
-- not "inert". That made the buff a real, narrowly classmask-scoped proc-consumable aura.
--
-- Confirmed via live debug instrumentation (backtraces + targeted log points added temporarily to
-- Unit.cpp/SpellAuras.cpp, since removed) that this was firing:
-- - On every Arcane Barrage cast - redundant with spell_mage_arcane_barrage::HandleAfterCast's own
--   intentional removal (Arcane Barrage's real classmask happens to match the pulled spell_proc
--   row's restriction), so functionally harmless there, but still unintended.
-- - On every Arcane Missiles cast too - "Arcane Missiles still consumes the Arcane Blast debuff"
--   despite the earlier System Rulings clarification that only Arcane Barrage and Temporal
--   Convergence should drop stacks. The exact statement responsible got lost to compiler inlining
--   across several debug rebuilds, but it reliably fired in the same instant the engine evaluated
--   (and correctly rejected, via classmask) 36032 for a proc off the Arcane Missiles cast - strongly
--   implicating this same live-proc-entry misconfiguration rather than anything in this rework's
--   own script code (which was already re-verified to touch 36032 nowhere near Arcane Missiles).
--
-- Reverting all three fields to 0/unset (matching every other spell in this file, and what this
-- buff always should have been) removes it from proc evaluation entirely, which fixes the Arcane
-- Barrage redundancy for certain and is the leading fix for the Arcane Missiles case.
--
-- Produced by `python3 apps/dbc-tools/generate.py`, hand-extracted to just this one row - see
-- rev_1788921755015417344.sql's header for why (full runs reproduce a large pre-existing,
-- unrelated diff across every class).

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` = 36032;
